    "['mpls l2vpn', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols l2circuit', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols l2circuit', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols l2circuit\\n##\\n\\nThe `mpls l2vpn` command in Huawei enables MPLS L2VPN functionality globally. In Juniper, the equivalent is `set protocols l2circuit`, which enables Layer 2 Circuit (the Juniper equivalent of MPLS L2VPN) functionality.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols l2circuit'}]]": 1,
    "['bidirectional static-cr-lsp ingress [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI `bidirectional static-cr-lsp ingress Tunnel10` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 ingress\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, bidirectional static LSPs are configured differently than in HUAWEI. The above commands create a bidirectional static LSP named \"Tunnel10\" with ingress properties. The complete configuration would require additional parameters (like next-hop and labels) which are specified separately in Juniper\\'s configuration structure.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 ingress', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 ingress', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI `bidirectional static-cr-lsp ingress Tunnel10` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 ingress\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, bidirectional static LSPs are configured differently than in HUAWEI. The above commands create a bidirectional static LSP named \"Tunnel10\" with ingress properties. The complete configuration would require additional parameters (like next-hop and labels) which are specified separately in Juniper\\'s configuration structure.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 ingress'}]]": 1,
    "['forward nexthop [parameter1] out-label [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-LSP-name transit 2.1.1.2 out-label 20', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI MPLS static CR-LSP forwarding configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-LSP-name transit 2.1.1.2 out-label 20\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, \"static-label-switched-path\" is used to configure static LSPs\\n- \"ingress-LSP-name\" would be replaced with the actual LSP name (comparable to \"Tunnel10\" in the original config)\\n- \"transit\" specifies the transit hop with next-hop IP and outbound label\\n- The parameters maintain the same values as the original (nexthop 2.1.1.2 and out-label 20)', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-LSP-name transit 2.1.1.2 out-label 20'}]]": 1,
    "['backward in-label [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path bidirectional-static-cr-lsp backward in-label 20', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 bidirectional', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `backward in-label 20`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path bidirectional-static-cr-lsp backward in-label 20\\n##\\n\\nThis Juniper command configures the incoming label (20) for the backward direction of a bidirectional static label-switched path, which corresponds to the HUAWEI bidirectional static CR-LSP configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path bidirectional-static-cr-lsp backward in-label 20'}]]": 1,
