    "['tnl-policy [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.3 interface ge-1/0/0.1 tunnel-policy tpatoc', 'parent_command': ['set system host-name [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set system host-name [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for `tnl-policy tpatoc`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.3 interface ge-1/0/0.1 tunnel-policy tpatoc\\n##\\n\\nThis Juniper command associates the tunnel policy \"tpatoc\" with the L2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.3 on interface ge-1/0/0.1, which is the equivalent functionality of the Huawei `tnl-policy tpatoc` command in the PW template context.\\n\\nNote: The exact interface name (ge-1/0/0.1) might need adjustment based on your Juniper device\\'s actual interface naming convention. The command assumes the same logical interface structure as in the Huawei configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols l2circuit neighbor 3.3.3.3 interface ge-1/0/0.1 tunnel-policy tpatoc'}]]": 1,
