    "['ip route-static [destination_address] [subnet_mask] [next_hop]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options static route 2.2.2.2/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the given Huawei static route:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-options static route 2.2.2.2/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n- Huawei's `ip route-static` becomes Juniper's `set routing-options static route`\\n- The destination and mask (2.2.2.2 255.255.255.255) are combined into CIDR notation (2.2.2.2/32)\\n- The next-hop address (2.1.1.2) remains the same but is specified with `next-hop` keyword\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-options static route 2.2.2.2/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2'}]]": 1,
    "['ip route-static [destination_ip] [destination_mask] [next_hop]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options static route 3.3.3.3/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the given Huawei static route:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-options static route 3.3.3.3/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2\\n##\\n\\nThis command:\\n1. Creates a static route for destination 3.3.3.3/32\\n2. Sets the next-hop as 2.1.1.2\\n3. Uses Juniper's configuration hierarchy format (routing-options > static > route)\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-options static route 3.3.3.3/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel-policy [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the HUAWEI `tunnel-policy` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, static LSPs are configured under `protocols mpls label-switched-path`\\n- The name `Tunnel10` is preserved as the LSP name\\n- The destination `2.2.2.2` matches the HUAWEI configuration\\'s tunnel binding destination\\n- Juniper doesn\\'t have an exact \"tunnel policy\" concept, but this creates the equivalent static LSP that will be used for the same purpose', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel binding destination [parameter1] te [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `tunnel binding destination` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2\\n##\\n\\nThis Juniper command establishes a static MPLS LSP named \"Tunnel10\" with the destination address 2.2.2.2, which is functionally equivalent to the HUAWEI tunnel binding configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2'}]]": 1,
    "['mpls-tp meg [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management meg test', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI `mpls-tp meg test` command:\\n\\n##\\nset oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management meg test\\n##\\n\\nThis Juniper command establishes an MPLS-TP Maintenance Entity Group (MEG) named \"test\" under CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) for OAM purposes, which is the equivalent functionality in Junos.', 'trans_template': 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management meg test'}]]": 1,
    "['me l2vc peer-ip [peer_ip] vc-id [vc_id] vc-type [vc_type] mep-id [mep_id] remote-mep-id [remote_mep_id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep 1 maintenance-domain test maintenance-association l2vc interface ge-1/0/0.1 vlan-id 1 peer 3.3.3.3 vc-id 30000 remote-mep 2', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management meg test'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper JUNOS configuration for the given HUAWEI MPLS-TP MEP (Maintenance End Point) configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep 1 maintenance-domain test maintenance-association l2vc interface ge-1/0/0.1 vlan-id 1 peer 3.3.3.3 vc-id 30000 remote-mep 2\\n##\\n\\nKey points about the translation:\\n1. Juniper uses CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) for similar functionality to Huawei\\'s MPLS-TP MEG configuration\\n2. The MEP ID (1), remote MEP ID (2), peer IP (3.3.3.3), and VC-ID (30000) are preserved\\n3. The VLAN-type is specified through the vlan-id parameter\\n4. The interface reference is converted to Juniper\\'s style (ge-1/0/0.1)\\n5. The maintenance domain name (\"test\" in this case) is carried over from the Huawei MEG name', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep 1 maintenance-domain test maintenance-association l2vc interface ge-1/0/0.1 vlan-id 1 peer 3.3.3.3 vc-id 30000 remote-mep 2'}]]": 1,
    "['cc send [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep continuity-check transmit interval 1ms', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management meg test'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for `cc send enable`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep continuity-check transmit interval 1ms\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Juniper, Continuity Check (CC) is part of the Ethernet Connectivity Fault Management (CFM) framework.\\n2. The command enables CC message transmission, similar to Huawei's `cc send enable`.\\n3. I included an interval (1ms) as Juniper requires this parameter, whereas Huawei defaults to 1s if unspecified.\\n4. The exact interval should match your network requirements.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep continuity-check transmit interval 1ms'}]]": 1,
    "['cc receive enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam eth-cfm maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test continuity-check transmission', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management meg test'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols oam eth-cfm maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test continuity-check transmission\\nset protocols oam eth-cfm maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test continuity-check reception\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `cc receive enable` command enables Continuity Check (CC) reception in MPLS-TP OAM for fault detection. The equivalent Juniper configuration uses Ethernet CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) with continuity-check parameters under the maintenance domain and association. Since Juniper doesn't have a direct 1:1 command, we configure both transmission and reception (which is typically enabled by default) to match the functionality.\\n\\nNote: Juniper's implementation uses a different OAM framework (ETH-CFM) compared to Huawei's MPLS-TP OAM, so the exact equivalence depends on the broader context of the MPLS-TP configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam eth-cfm maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test continuity-check transmission'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam eth-cfm maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test continuity-check reception', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management meg test'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols oam eth-cfm maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test continuity-check transmission\\nset protocols oam eth-cfm maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test continuity-check reception\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `cc receive enable` command enables Continuity Check (CC) reception in MPLS-TP OAM for fault detection. The equivalent Juniper configuration uses Ethernet CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) with continuity-check parameters under the maintenance domain and association. Since Juniper doesn't have a direct 1:1 command, we configure both transmission and reception (which is typically enabled by default) to match the functionality.\\n\\nNote: Juniper's implementation uses a different OAM framework (ETH-CFM) compared to Huawei's MPLS-TP OAM, so the exact equivalence depends on the broader context of the MPLS-TP configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam eth-cfm maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test continuity-check reception'}]]": 1,
    "['lost-measure dual-ended [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep test dual-ended loss-measurement', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep test dual-ended loss-measurement', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep test dual-ended loss-measurement \\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep test dual-ended loss-measurement'}]]": 1
